From 16a7011854f5c653121685eb2892a493909d147c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alantero <36408154+alantero@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:34:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Build and run on macOS (Apple Silicon) with the native
 renderer on MoltenVK

The native renderer's Vulkan backend on macOS, as one more POSIX system,
built with this CMake as on Linux:

- platform_posix.cpp: the macOS calls where Linux has its own (nanosleep,
  QoS classes, Mach thread times and reads, _NSGetExecutablePath, dyld's
  image list), and the window as the CAMetalLayer of an SDL Metal view.
- present.inc: the Vulkan surface of that layer (VK_EXT_metal_surface).
- backend.cpp: the loader and MoltenVK of the app's bundle, found as the
  SDK finds them, loaded before volk looks for the loader by name.
- app_entry.cpp, narutorise_app.h, supervisor.cpp: the executable's path,
  the restart's pipe and the supervised child without Linux-only calls,
  and std::min on operands of one type (size_t is not uint64_t there).
- controls/service.cpp: libc++ has no std::atomic<std::shared_ptr>, so a
  mutex guards the configuration where it is missing.
- plume-engine.cmake: Plume's Objective-C++ part and its frameworks.
- shader-cache.cmake: dxc-macos from dxc-bin, and the C compiler of
  XenosRecomp from /usr/bin/c++.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
